WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.492
Module 12 answered the question, can we trust the data?

00:00:04.492 --> 00:00:10.307
Module 13 asks the next question: what does the data tell us?

00:00:10.307 --> 00:00:16.192
Once values are consistently coded and obvious quality problems are addressed,

00:00:16.192 --> 00:00:20.030
we can use statistics and charts with much more confidence.

00:00:20.491 --> 00:00:27.618
We will move from descriptive summaries into distributions, group comparisons, scatter plots, correlation,

00:00:27.618 --> 00:00:32.687
and a simple introduction to confidence intervals.

00:00:32.687 --> 00:00:36.837
Statistics and visualization work best together.

00:00:36.837 --> 00:00:40.282
A summary table gives us exact values.

00:00:40.282 --> 00:00:43.917
A chart makes patterns easier to see.

00:00:43.917 --> 00:00:51.007
After this module, Module 14 will introduce machine learning and external data.

00:00:51.007 --> 00:00:58.367
The ideas here are important preparation because machine learning also depends on understanding distributions,

00:00:58.367 --> 00:01:02.562
relationships, and variation before fitting a model.
